## ZeroAI's six core primitives

### 1. Intent Contract

Turn natural language into a typed contract before execution.

```ts
type IntentContract = {
  goal: string
  constraints: string[]
  acceptanceCriteria: AcceptanceCriterion[]
  permissions: Permission[]
  resources: ResourceRef[]
  riskLevel: "low" | "medium" | "high"
}
```

The model can interpret the request.

The runtime owns the contract.

---

### 2. Task Graph

Never rely on the AI to remember the workflow.

```text
Understand request
     ↓
Inspect current state
     ↓
Plan changes
     ↓
Execute
     ↓
Test
     ↓
Verify evidence
     ↓
Certify
```

Each node has:

```ts
{
  id,
  dependencies,
  owner,
  inputs,
  expectedOutputs,
  timeout,
  retryPolicy,
  permissions,
  acceptanceGate
}
```

That makes execution resumable and deterministic.

---

### 3. Agent Registry

Agents are capabilities, not personalities.

```ts
type AgentDefinition = {
  id: string
  version: string
  responsibilities: string[]
  allowedTools: string[]
  forbiddenActions: string[]
  inputSchema: ZodSchema
  outputSchema: ZodSchema
  instructionSet: string
}
```

Example agents:

```text
architect
frontend
backend
database
security
qa
release
research
seo
operations
```

The model behind any agent can change without changing the architecture.

